    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/ea7e5234b27bdfd50507bc740b598945-problem-solving.png",
    "display_name": "Planning for a User",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Build a user persona, identify their key need, and write a focused problem statement.",
    "teacher_markdown": "* Students often jump straight to solutions (“They need an app that sends reminders”). Redirect them to focus on the need behind the solution. Ask: “What is the person struggling with underneath that?” or “Why does that matter to them?”\r\n\r\n* If personas feel generic (“a student who is busy”), push for specificity. Encourage details that make the person real — schedule constraints, emotional reactions, or situational barriers. Strong problem statements come from specific people, not vague users."
  },
